  "description": "Hack the Hardware – National Hardware Innovation Challenge Ideas are only the beginning. The real challenge lies in engineering them into working solutions. HACK THE HARDWARE is a national-level hardware innovation challenge organised as part of TECHNEX 2026 , the 20th edition of the annual technical festival of St. Vincent Pallotti College of Engineering & Technology, Nagpur. The competition brings together students, hardware enthusiasts, makers, and aspiring engineers to tackle real-world engineering problems through practical implementation, rapid prototyping, and system integration. Unlike conventional coding competitions, this challenge focuses on building tangible solutions by combining hardware, electronics, embedded systems, sensors, actuators, software, and engineering design. Challenge Domains 1. Healthcare & Assistive Technology Develop hardware-based solutions for healthcare monitoring, patient assistance, rehabilitation, biomedical instrumentation, wearable health devices and accessibility for people with disabilities. 2. Smart Mobility & Automotive Technology Build innovative solutions for electric vehicles, intelligent transportation, vehicle safety, autonomous mobility, smart traffic management, and automotive electronics. 3. Industrial Automation Explore automation, control systems, smart monitoring, industrial processes, and intelligent manufacturing solutions. 4. Agriculture & Environment Build technology-driven solutions addressing agricultural challenges, resource management, environmental monitoring, and sustainability. 5. Safety & Disaster Management Develop practical solutions for hazard detection, emergency response, monitoring, safety systems, and disaster preparedness. Venue: St. Vincent Pallotti College of Engineering & Technology, Nagpur, Maharashtra. Event Dates: 19–20 December 2026. Bring your ideas, your engineering skills, and your willingness to build. The challenge is to turn imagination into something that works.",
