    "details": "<p><strong>Hack the Hardware &ndash; National Hardware Innovation Challenge</strong></p>\n<p>Ideas are only the beginning. The real challenge lies in engineering them into working solutions.</p>\n<p>HACK THE HARDWARE is a national-level hardware innovation challenge organised as part of <strong>TECHNEX 2026</strong>, the 20th edition of the annual technical festival of St. Vincent Pallotti College of Engineering &amp; Technology, Nagpur.</p>\n<p>The competition brings together students, hardware enthusiasts, makers, and aspiring engineers to tackle real-world engineering problems through practical implementation, rapid prototyping, and system integration.</p>\n<p>Unlike conventional coding competitions, this challenge focuses on building tangible solutions by combining hardware, electronics, embedded systems, sensors, actuators, software, and engineering design.</p>\n<h3>Challenge Domains</h3>\n<p><strong>1. Healthcare &amp; Assistive Technology</strong><br />Develop hardware-based solutions for healthcare monitoring, patient assistance, rehabilitation, biomedical instrumentation, wearable health devices and accessibility for people with disabilities.</p>\n<p><strong>2. Smart Mobility &amp; Automotive Technology</strong><br />Build innovative solutions for electric vehicles, intelligent transportation, vehicle safety, autonomous mobility, smart traffic management, and automotive electronics.</p>\n<p><strong>3. Industrial Automation</strong><br />Explore automation, control systems, smart monitoring, industrial processes, and intelligent manufacturing solutions.</p>\n<p><strong>4. Agriculture &amp; Environment</strong><br />Build technology-driven solutions addressing agricultural challenges, resource management, environmental monitoring, and sustainability.</p>\n<p><strong>5. Safety &amp; Disaster Management</strong> <br />Develop practical solutions for hazard detection, emergency response, monitoring, safety systems, and disaster preparedness.</p>\n<p><strong>Venue:</strong> St. Vincent Pallotti College of Engineering &amp; Technology, Nagpur, Maharashtra.</p>\n<p><strong>Event Dates:</strong> 19&ndash;20 December 2026.</p>\n<p>Bring your ideas, your engineering skills, and your willingness to build. The challenge is to turn imagination into something that works.</p>",
